    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6462fb5e-e032-5691-b3e8-e7333072b5af" activityNameId="64729a22-f3df-5d74-889d-d2acd14c603c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Avoided burden from recycling, CdTe PV module</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Avoided burden from recycling, CdTe PV module
This dataset is based on information on the amount of recovered materials provided by Parikhit Sinha, First Solar. The benefits for recovery of waste glass are modelled based on information from Held and Ilg (2011) and KBOB LCI data DQRv2:2016. It is assumed that 90% of the glass and 100% of the metals are recovered.;
UUID: d11d3fc9-cd92-48f6-b955-d4e5f95a0a6c
This dataset includes the benefits for the avoided production of glass, aluminium, copper and semiconductor by the  recycling of cadmium telluride photovoltaic panels.
Location: Germany
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature data. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_d11d3fc9-cd92-48f6-b955-d4e5f95a0a6c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
